node_modules/
dist/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.local
.DS_Store

# Third-party agent skills installed with `npx skills add` (taste-skill,
# impeccable, emilkowalski/skills). Local design tooling, not part of the
# product: ~3.9 MB of code that the installer itself warns "runs with full
# agent permissions", which does not belong in a repository whose stated
# posture is zero runtime dependencies. Anyone who wants them runs one command.
/.agents/
/.claude/skills/*
!/.claude/skills/trazum/

# Lockfile for third-party agent skills; see .gitignore
skills-lock.json

# The .vsix `npm run package:vscode` writes.
#
# The packaging step produces an installable file beside the extension, and the
# guard against runtime state in this repository checks the *tracked* tree — an
# untracked artefact is somebody's local mess. That is the right rule and it is
# also how a binary gets in: `git add -A` before a commit sweeps up whatever the
# last command left behind, which is exactly how sixty waiver records reached
# `main` and sat there for two releases. Ignored so the documented command
# cannot cost somebody that.
*.vsix
